 To find $f(600)$, we can use the given property of the function $f(xy) = f(x)/y$. Since we know $f(500) = 3$, we can set $x = 500$ and $y = 1.2$ because $500 \times 1.2 = 600$. Thus, $f(600) = f(500 \times 1.2) = f(500)/1.2 = 3/1.2 = 2.5$.

@Carol Wayne: How can I type math symbols like √ using my keyboard?
To type mathematical symbols such as square roots on a standard keyboard, you can use LaTeX formatting. For example, to type the square root of x, you would write $\sqrt{x}$. This will render as $\sqrt{x}$ when the page is refreshed. You can learn more by referring to a LaTeX guide or a math markup help function in your document.

